      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# TEST: EPS Distributor - one image, three branches, each on/off\n\n**Just press Run.** No checkpoint, no lora, no GPU, no setup - it only moves\none image around. Takes a second.\n\n## Pass 1 - everything on (how it ships)\n\nPress **Run** once with all three toggles ON. You should get:\n\n- `output/eps_disttest/branch_A_00001_.png` - the plain image\n- `output/eps_disttest/branch_B_inverted_00001_.png` - **colour-inverted**\n- a preview of the image on the `PreviewImage` node at the bottom\n\nThat is three branches off ONE image in ONE run. Nothing ran twice.\n\n## Pass 2 - turn a branch off (the actual test)\n\nClick the little **checkbox next to `out_2`** on the EPS Distributor so it\ngoes dark, then press **Run** again. Now:\n\n- `branch_A_00002_.png` appears - branch A still runs\n- **NO new `branch_B_inverted_` file** - branch B was skipped\n- the preview still updates - branch C still runs\n\nThe important part: the **Invert** node in the middle of branch B never\nexecuted either. A disabled output skips the WHOLE chain hanging off it, not\njust the node touching it. Watch the canvas during Run - Invert never\nhighlights.\n\n## Pass 3 - all off is legal\n\nTurn all three off (or use the **Toggle All** box in the node's header) and\npress Run. The queue should finish **successfully** with nothing new written\nand no error. That is intended: an all-off Distributor simply means nothing\ndownstream of it runs this time.\n\n## Also worth a click\n\n- **Right-click the node -> Properties -> `Outputs`** to show more than three\n  (up to 8) or fewer. Only sockets at the BOTTOM are added or removed, so the\n  wires you already have never jump to a different output.\n- Try lowering `Outputs` to **1** while `out_2` is still wired: it should\n  **refuse** to go below 2 and tell you `out_2` is wired. Unwire it first and\n  it will go all the way down.\n"
      ],
